  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Space** (1 review): Reviewer found Space rather dull; nearby audience chatter was minimal, just a little chirping [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Take Off from Haight Ashbury**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Old News Broadcast of the Grateful Dead**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-05-17.TheSphereVegas2024DeadCo** (recommended): audience recording; 21 songs; 197 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the recording crystal clear with plenty of bass, and says it conveys the drums vividly [3]\n- **deadco2024-05-17**: source not stated; 21 songs; 197 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Taped from the taper section, section 103, row 36, with mics held six feet high [1]\n- Karl Perazzo sat in as special guest [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-05-17.TheSphereVegas2024DeadCo**: taped by JT/NY; transferred by JT/NY; source: Aud > Schoeps CCM 41's > Lemo Cables > MixPre 6 > SD @ 32/48 [1]. Also: Reviewer thinks this was taper JT's first attempt at recording inside the Sphere; Audience recording: Schoeps CCM 41V mics, Lemo cables, MixPre 6 to SD at 32-bit/48k; edited in Sound Forge Pro 16, converted to FLAC with Traders Little Helper [1][3]\n- **deadco2024-05-17**: taped by Eric Lugassy; transferred by Eric Lugassy; source: Channels 1 & 2: B9 C31F > NBob Active Cables > Baby Nbox > Channels 3 & 4: AT3031 Cardioids 6\" apart > Zoom F6 32 Bit Float [2]. Also: Eric Lugassy both taped and transferred this recording, under the handles Hunter S and Tire Iron; Rig used B9 C31F mics through NBob active cables and Baby Nbox, plus AT3031 cardioids six inches apart; SD to WAV to Reaper to 24-bit FLAC [2]",
